  "note": "The thermal root has |k_th| = sqrt(omega/2/kappa), i.e. it is a diffusion branch.  Its ratio to the acoustic wavenumber falls as omega^(-1/2) and only reaches 1 near 1e11-1e12 Hz, where the continuum and Fourier assumptions have already failed.  Over any band a transducer or ultrasonic measurement can address, the thermal root is never a propagating far-field channel."
 },
