  "seven_condition_analysis": {
   "advertised": 7,
   "required_for_deg8": 8,
   "deficit": 1,
   "explanation": "The blueprint states that the closest prior art already uses seven interface conditions for two piezothermoelastic half-spaces.  For the four-field model the k_z polynomial has degree eight, so a welded interface must impose eight scalar conditions (u_x, u_z, s_xz, s_zz, phi, D_z, theta, q_z) and a two-half-space problem has eight unknowns (four reflected, four transmitted).  Seven is therefore one short.  Two readings are possible and only the source paper can settle which applies: either the blueprint has mischaracterised the prior art, or that formulation fixes one field by an extra assumption that must be identified and carried over.  The three-region problem needs sixteen conditions either way, so the count cannot be inherited from the two-half-space case."
  },
  "note": "The count is set by the polynomial degree, not by the number of physical fields, and it is not eight by assumption: a two-temperature or heat-flux-vector formulation raises it to ten and changes the interface conditions themselves."
 },
