  "note": "Dimension check: eps = beta^2 T0/(rho c_v M_L) with M_L = rho c_L^2 the longitudinal modulus and rho c_v the volumetric heat capacity, hence dimensionless; an earlier draft divided by rho c_v c_L^2 only and returned eps ~ 24, which is the check that caught it.  eps is of order 1e-3 to 1e-2, so temperature shifts the mechanical branch by a fraction of a percent.  The thermal root is diffusive (Part A), so its effect on a travelling longitudinal wave is an ATTENUATION of order 1e-9 to 1e-4 Np/mm at ultrasonic frequencies.  The temperature field therefore adds no propagating branch and no measurable absorption at the intended scale: the four-field and three-field power budgets are identical to well beyond plotting accuracy."
 },
